{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md | sed -n '178,196p'\"","aggregated_output":"   178\t8. **Code simplify:** Run /simplify against the changed files. \n   179\t\n   180\t9. **Security review:** If the diff touches auth, secrets, user input, network boundaries, or filesystem trust boundaries (copying/moving/promoting files between directories, extracting archives, sandbox-to-production transfers), run /security. Otherwise \"N/A.\"\n   181\t\n   182\t10. **Contract assertions:** Mark each assertion PASS, FAIL, or SKIP with a one-line explanation. SKIPs for work deferred to later tasks: append to `mission/deferrals.md` as `task N -- <assertion>`.\n   183\t\n   184\t11. **Behavioral conformance:** For each assertion that describes observable behavior (CLI output, exit codes, file content, API response, shell behavior), write and execute a minimal test script that verifies the behavior by actually running the code. Do not rely solely on reading the code -- run it. Examples:\n   185\t    - CLI flag assertion: run the binary with the flag, check output\n   186\t    - Exit code assertion: run the command, check `$?`\n   187\t    - Shell alias assertion: source the alias, run `type <name>`, check the definition\n   188\t    - API response assertion: curl the endpoint, check the response body\n   189\t    \n   190\t    If an assertion cannot be tested via execution (e.g., internal architecture, code organization, build configuration), mark it as \"verified by inspection\" with an explanation of why execution was not possible.\n   191\t    \n   192\t    If a behavioral test is inconclusive (e.g., the test script errors out, the environment lacks a dependency), mark it as \"verified by inspection (execution inconclusive: <reason>)\" and fall back to code reading. Do not let an inconclusive execution check block the validation.\n   193\t    \n   194\t    Report each assertion's verification method (execution or inspection) in the contract assertions table.\n   195\t\n   196\t12. **Silent skip detection:** Grep test files in the diff for language-specific patterns that cause tests to report PASS while testing nothing. Use the `Detected language` named fact from the deterministic pre-pass to choose the primary language-specific scan, and also inspect file extensions in the diff so mixed-language projects are covered.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
