{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design-decisions.md | sed -n '30,235p'\"","aggregated_output":"    30\t- Do NOT receive the contract (adversarial separation)\n    31\t- Do NOT receive previous workers' handoff reports (clean context)\n    32\t- Commit all work in a single commit\n    33\t- Write a structured handoff report to disk\n    34\t- Default engine: Codex (configurable in mission/config.yaml)\n    35\t\n    36\t### Per-task validators (run sequentially)\n    37\t1. **Scrutiny validator** -- test presence gate, build/test/lint, /review, code standards, /simplify, /security (conditional), contract assertions. Always runs.\n    38\t2. **User-test validator** -- decides API tests (HTTP) and/or browser tests (agent-browser) based on what changed. Always runs.\n    39\t3. **Demo video** -- recorded after both validators pass, for frontend tasks. Orchestrator decides when.\n    40\t\n    41\t### End-of-mission review\n    42\t4. **Dual adversarial review** -- runs once after the draft PR is created, against the full diff. Codex and Claude independently review the code. Both reports are presented to the human. No automated fix loop -- the human decides what to address.\n    43\t\n    44\tValidators receive: commit SHA + contract assertions. They do NOT receive proposal, design, or worker reasoning.\n    45\t\n    46\t### Fix Loop\n    47\t- On validation failure: orchestrator writes a symptom-based fix brief (no contract text) to mission/issues/, spawns a fix worker\n    48\t- Fix worker uses `/tdd` to fix\n    49\t- Fix worker commits a single fix commit\n    50\t- Both per-task validators re-run after every fix (scrutiny + user-test)\n    51\t- Circuit breaker: 3 attempts on the same task -> pause and ask human\n    52\t- Skipped tasks marked with `- [~]` in tasks.md -- the build loop ignores them\n    53\t\n    54\t## Key Design Decisions\n    55\t\n    56\t### Bash run_in_background for external processes\n    57\t- Long-running external processes (Codex workers, Codex adversarial reviews) run via Bash with `run_in_background: true`, with stdout+stderr redirected to a log file under `mission/logs/`\n    58\t- Claude subagent validators use the Agent tool directly since they run within the session\n    59\t- The log file lets the human watch progress in another terminal (`tail -f`) without the agent paying context cost for mid-run events\n    60\t\n    61\t### File-backed state\n    62\t- All mission state lives on disk in the mission directory\n    63\t- The orchestrator reads fresh state before each cycle (survives compaction)\n    64\t- Enables session resume if Claude Code dies\n    65\t- tmux as first line of defense against session death\n    66\t\n    67\t### Serial execution\n    68\t- One worker at a time (matches Factory's approach)\n    69\t- Parallelization only for read-only operations within validators\n    70\t- Correctness compounds over time\n    71\t\n    72\t### Vertical slices\n    73\t- Each task in tasks.md should be a thin vertical slice cutting through all layers\n    74\t- A completed task is demoable and verifiable on its own\n    75\t- One task = one worker = one commit = one validation cycle\n    76\t\n    77\t### Configurable engines\n    78\t- mission/config.yaml specifies which engine per role (codex/claude)\n    79\t- Default: Codex for workers and adversarial reviewer A, Claude for validators, adversarial reviewer B, and demo video\n    80\t- Swap engines when new models drop without changing anything else\n    81\t\n    82\t### OpenSpec integration\n    83\t- `/mission` is the single workflow for all work (small fixes to large epics). Scope adapts naturally.\n    84\t- contract.md is a new OpenSpec artifact (validation assertions, written during planning)\n    85\t- mission/ directory nests inside openspec/changes/<change-name>/\n    86\t- Archiving the change archives the mission artifacts too\n    87\t\n    88\t### Entry point and completion\n    89\t- `/mission` skill starts a mission\n    90\t- `/mission-resume` resumes from file state\n    91\t- `/mission-status` shows progress\n    92\t- On completion: draft PR created via `gh pr create --draft`\n    93\t- Human reviews and promotes to ready\n    94\t\n    95\t## Orchestrator Plan Structure\n    96\t\n    97\t```markdown\n    98\t# Mission: [change-name]\n    99\t\n   100\t## State Directory\n   101\topenspec/changes/<change-name>/mission/\n   102\t\n   103\t## OpenSpec Artifacts\n   104\t- Proposal: openspec/changes/<change-name>/proposal.md\n   105\t- Design: openspec/changes/<change-name>/design.md\n   106\t- Tasks: openspec/changes/<change-name>/tasks.md\n   107\t- Contract: openspec/changes/<change-name>/contract.md\n   108\t\n   109\t## Engine Config\n   110\t- Workers: codex\n   111\t- Scrutiny validator: claude\n   112\t- User-test validator: claude\n   113\t- Adversarial reviewer A: codex\n   114\t- Adversarial reviewer B: claude\n   115\t- Demo video: claude\n   116\t\n   117\t## Skills to Use\n   118\t- Alignment: /grill (during planning, before artifacts are created)\n   119\t- Shared language: /language (during planning, establish terms)\n   120\t- PRD: /prd (turn grill conversation into structured PRD)\n   121\t- Planning: /opsx:propose (create proposal, design, tasks from PRD)\n   122\t- Task breakdown: each task is a vertical slice through all layers, demoable and verifiable on its own\n   123\t- Contract: written by orchestrator after planning, before workers start\n   124\t- Worker implementation: /tdd (test-driven development for workers)\n   125\t- Worker briefs: assembled from proposal.md + design.md + task description\n   126\t- Scrutiny validation: build/test/lint + /review + /simplify against contract\n   127\t- Security validation: /security (for tasks touching auth/sensitive paths)\n   128\t- User-test validation: /test-app (agent-browser) and/or HTTP tests against API\n   129\t- Adversarial review: dual Codex + Claude review in parallel, orchestrator synthesizes\n   130\t- Demo video: /demo-video (for frontend tasks)\n   131\t- Completion: gh pr create --draft (draft PR with mission summary)\n   132\t- Archival: /opsx:archive (after merge)\n   133\t\n   134\t## Mission Flow\n   135\tFor each unchecked task in tasks.md:\n   136\t1. Read mission state from mission/progress.md\n   137\t2. Write brief to mission/briefs/task-N.md\n   138\t3. Kick off worker via Bash `run_in_background` (engine per config.yaml)\n   139\t4. On completion, read mission/handoffs/task-N.md\n   140\t5. Spawn scrutiny validator (commit SHA + contract assertions)\n   141\t6. If fail -> write symptom-based fix brief, spawn fix worker, re-validate both. Circuit breaker: 3 attempts -> ask human.\n   142\t7. Spawn user-test validator (commit SHA + contract assertions)\n   143\t8. If fail -> same fix/re-validate loop\n   144\t9. If frontend task -> spawn demo video\n   145\t10. Mark task complete in tasks.md, update progress.md\n   146\t\n   147\tAfter all tasks complete:\n   148\t11. Create draft PR\n   149\t12. Run dual adversarial review (Codex + Claude) against full diff\n   150\t13. Present both reports to human alongside PR link\n   151\t\n   152\t## Rules\n   153\t- One worker at a time (serial execution)\n   154\t- Workers never see contract.md\n   155\t- Validators never see proposal.md or design.md\n   156\t- On any failure, re-run BOTH validators after fix\n   157\t- Write all decisions to progress.md\n   158\t```\n   159\t\n   160\t## Mission Directory Structure\n   161\t\n   162\t```\n   163\topenspec/changes/<change-name>/\n   164\t  .openspec.yaml\n   165\t  proposal.md\n   166\t  design.md\n   167\t  tasks.md\n   168\t  contract.md\n   169\t  mission/\n   170\t    config.yaml\n   171\t    progress.md\n   172\t    briefs/\n   173\t      task-1.md\n   174\t      task-2.md\n   175\t    handoffs/\n   176\t      task-1.md\n   177\t      task-2.md\n   178\t    validations/\n   179\t      task-1-scrutiny.md\n   180\t      task-1-usertest.md\n   181\t      task-1-demo.mp4\n   182\t    issues/\n   183\t      task-1-v1.md\n   184\t```\n   185\t\n   186\t## Worker Brief Format\n   187\t\n   188\t```markdown\n   189\t# Worker Brief: Task N - [name]\n   190\t\n   191\t## Your Task\n   192\t[Task description and acceptance criteria]\n   193\t\n   194\t## Project Context\n   195\t[Relevant excerpt from proposal.md]\n   196\t\n   197\t## Architecture\n   198\t[Relevant excerpt from design.md]\n   199\t\n   200\t## Procedures\n   201\t- Implement the task as described\n   202\t- Commit all changes in a single commit with message: \"[task-N] description\"\n   203\t- Write your handoff report to mission/handoffs/task-N.md using the format below\n   204\t\n   205\t## Handoff Report Format\n   206\t- Task: [which task]\n   207\t- Commit SHA: [the SHA]\n   208\t- Approach: [brief explanation of what you did and why]\n   209\t- Commands run: [build/test/lint commands and exit codes]\n   210\t- Concerns: [anything you're uncertain about]\n   211\t```\n   212\t\n   213\t## Contract Format\n   214\t\n   215\t```markdown\n   216\t# Contract\n   217\t\n   218\t## Task 1: [name]\n   219\t- [Assertion verifiable from outside without knowing the code]\n   220\t- [Another assertion]\n   221\t\n   222\t## Task 2: [name]\n   223\t- [Assertion]\n   224\t```\n   225\t\n   226\t## Fix Brief Format\n   227\t\n   228\t```markdown\n   229\t# Fix Brief: Task N - [name] (Attempt 2)\n   230\t\n   231\t## What Failed\n   232\t[Specific failed assertions from the validator report]\n   233\t\n   234\t## Validator Output\n   235\t[Relevant error messages, test failures, review findings]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
